A cast's start held by the log's Stagger breaks' holds without a cast event (2026-11-27, the break's open points; dropped)

On top of break-hold-place (e5bf988): the placement's pass-2 stops take the logged breaks' holds (holds.ts breakStops,
from breakHoldStarts), and a new cast's start (logcasts.ts newCastStart) moves earlier by every break-hold frame
between it and its first landing, with or without the log's cast event (every clock stands in a break's hold; a
landing inside one is the breaker's own, logged inside its hold). The cases: fc63a2001251 Typhoeus's 99.03 s combo
across the 101.11 s break (INSIDE at 102.33 s), 3aa6ab93bad4 Zhuang Fangyi's 145.63 s combo (INSIDE at 145.73 s).
Measured (measure --patch --base HEAD at e5bf988): development 3 better (4360, 9090, a27b +1 plain each), 1 mixed
(00ae −2 plain: hidden holds placed elsewhere), earlier pending d4fb mixed (plain 843 → 850, mismatch 10 → 11), d774
worse (damage −0.4 → −0.5%), hold-outs 2 worse (plain −12, assumed +5, unquantified +4, mismatch +2; plain 82.5 →
82.3%), no decision kind's count moved there. Dropped on the hold-outs. In another agent's file (logcasts.ts) too.

